  "own_original_text": "ErecutF'e Oter\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by law, the Executive Order of\nOctober 22, 1916, providing for the payment of interest on deposit money\norders issued in the Canal zone, is hereby amended to read as follows:\ni. Deposit money orders issued by the Canal Zone Postal Service shall\nbear interest at the rate of three-fourths of one percentum for each period of\nthree full calendar months, from January i, 1923, or subsequent date of issue.\nInterest shall be payable when the order is paid but shall not accrue on any\norder for more than three years.\n2. On deposit money orders issued prior to January 1, 1923, interest will\nbe paid as specified in Executive Order of October 22, 19 16, except that interest\nfor the period or periods of three full calendar months, ending subsequent to\nDecember 31, 1922, shah be paid at the rate of three fourths of one percentumi\nfor each of such periods.\n3. The Governor of The Panama Canal is authorized to prescribe such\ndetailed rules and regulations as may be necessary to carry out this order.\nWARREN G HARD ING\nTanII WHITE HoUSE,\nDec. 6, 1922.\n[No. 3761.]\nCovIsCm t I (TI!(Go IT K1\n1/\na{ pe led\n'hi\n4b",
